## How to Run

Open the terminal in the 'Assignment 1' folder.

### Assignment 1
Compile:
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic \
  main.cpp Map.cpp Cell.cpp Tower.cpp \
  DirectDamageTower.cpp AreaDamageTower.cpp \
  SlowTower.cpp Critter.cpp CritterGroup.cpp \
  CritterGroupGenerator.cpp Player.cpp Tests.cpp \
  -o tower_defense.exe

Run:
./tower_defense.exe

The original program includes 14 tests.

### Assignment 2 — Observer Pattern GUIs
The graphical demonstrations use SFML 3. Compile each GUI separately.

The commands below assume SFML is installed through Homebrew on macOS.

#### 1. Map Observer
Compile:
clang++ -std=c++17 gui_main.cpp MapObserver.cpp \
  Map.cpp Cell.cpp \
  -isysroot "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)" \
  -isystem "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)/usr/include/c++/v1" \
  -I/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/include \
  -L/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/lib \
  -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system \
  -o tower_defense_map_gui

Run:
./tower_defense_map_gui

#### 2. Tower Observer
Compile:
clang++ -std=c++17 tower_gui_main.cpp \
  TowerObserver.cpp Tower.cpp DirectDamageTower.cpp \
  Player.cpp Critter.cpp \
  -isysroot "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)" \
  -isystem "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)/usr/include/c++/v1" \
  -I/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/include \
  -L/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/lib \
  -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system \
  -o tower_defense_tower_gui

Run:
./tower_defense_tower_gui

#### 3. Critter Observer
Compile:
clang++ -std=c++17 critter_gui_main.cpp \
  CritterObserver.cpp Critter.cpp \
  -isysroot "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)" \
  -isystem "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)/usr/include/c++/v1" \
  -I/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/include \
  -L/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/lib \
  -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system \
  -o tower_defense_critter_gui

Run:
./tower_defense_critter_gui

#### 4. Critter Group Observer
Compile:
clang++ -std=c++17 critter_group_gui_main.cpp \
  CritterGroupObserver.cpp CritterGroup.cpp Critter.cpp \
  -isysroot "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)" \
  -isystem "$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)/usr/include/c++/v1" \
  -I/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/include \
  -L/opt/homebrew/opt/sfml/lib \
  -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system \
  -o tower_defense_group_gui

Run:
./tower_defense_group_gui

## Observer Pattern Overview
The Observer pattern allows observable objects to notify registered observers when relevant changes occur.

- `Observer.h` defines the observer interface.
- `Observable.h` manages observer registration, removal, and notifications.
- `MapObserver` displays the map.
- `TowerObserver` displays tower information.
- `CritterObserver` displays critter information.
- `CritterGroupObserver` displays the critter group and its members.

The Assignment 1 program and Assignment 2 graphical demonstrations use separate driver programs and must be compiled separately.

## Requirements

- A C++17-compatible compiler.
- SFML 3 for the graphical demonstrations.
- On macOS, the compile commands above assume Homebrew SFML and the Apple Command Line Tools.
